    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "yeah but that's the thing... what if it's not a \"medical issue\" with the real alex? i've seen these theories online about how high-profile people get replaced by these hyper-realistic sims or lookalikes when they \"retire\" or something. and when you look at the \"glitches\" i mentioned—the blink timing, the dead eyes, the weirdly perfect skin—it doesn't feel like a brain issue, it feels like a rendering issue. like, if you had to bet, do those weird behavioral anomalies look more like a person with a neurological problem or a synthetic entity that's just not quite calibrated right?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
